  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000004",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Lattice energy",
    "reading_order" : 4,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 4,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000005",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "As with bond enthalpy, **lattice energy **(Δ<sub>*latt*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup>) can be expressed as a formation or dissociation process",
    "reading_order" : 5,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000006",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "As a formation process, it is the enthalpy change when **1 mole** of an **ionic compound **is formed from its **gaseous ions **(under standard conditions)",
    "reading_order" : 6,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000007",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The Δ<sub>*latt*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup> is therefore **exothermic, **as when ions are **combined** to form an **ionic solid lattice **there is an extremely large release of energy",
    "reading_order" : 7,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000008",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Since this is an exothermic process, the enthalpy change will have a **negative** value",
    "reading_order" : 8,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000009",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Because of the huge release in energy when the gaseous ions combine, the value will be a very **large negative** value",
    "reading_order" : 9,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000010",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The large negative value of Δ<sub>*latt*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup> suggests that the **ionic compound **is much more **stable **than its **gaseous ions**",
    "reading_order" : 10,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000011",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This is due to the **strong electrostatic forces of attraction **between the oppositely charged ions in the solid lattice",
    "reading_order" : 11,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000012",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Since there are no electrostatic forces of attraction between the ions in the gas phase, the gaseous ions are **less stable **than the ions in the **ionic lattice**",
    "reading_order" : 12,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000013",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **more exothermic** the value is, the **stronger the ionic bonds** within the lattice are",
    "reading_order" : 13,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000014",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The Δ<sub>*latt*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup> of an ionic compound **cannot **be determined **directly **by one single experiment",
    "reading_order" : 14,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000015",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Multiple experimental values and an **energy cycle **are used to find the Δ<sub>*latt*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup> of ionic compounds",
    "reading_order" : 15,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000016",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The lattice energy (Δ<sub>*latt*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup>) of an ionic compound can be written as an equation",
    "reading_order" : 16,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000017",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "For example, sodium chloride is an ionic compound formed from sodium (Na<sup>+</sup>) and chloride (C*l*<sup>-</sup>) ions",
    "reading_order" : 17,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000018",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
