  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000039",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The **standard** **enthalpy change of atomisation **(Δ<sub>*at*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup>) is the **enthalpy change** when **1 mole of gaseous atoms **is formed from its **element **under standard conditions",
    "reading_order" : 39,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000040",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The Δ<sub>*at*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ </sup>is always **endothermic **as energy is always required to **break** any bonds between the atoms in the element, to break the element into its gaseous atoms",
    "reading_order" : 40,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000041",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Since this is always an endothermic process, the enthalpy change will always have a **positive** value",
    "reading_order" : 41,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000042",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Equations can be written to show the standard enthalpy change of atomisation (Δ<sub>*at*</sub>*H*<sup>ꝋ</sup>) for elements",
    "reading_order" : 42,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
